<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Berlin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1878</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Berlin (1878) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1877-1878">Russo-Turkish War (1877–1878)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> was a meeting of the great powers chaired by Bismarck in June and July 1878 to revise the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-san-stefano">Treaty of San Stefano</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1877-1878">Russo-Turkish War</a>. It recognised the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, Montenegro and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, creating Eastern Rumelia, and let <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> occupy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin.jpg" alt="Congress of Berlin" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton von Werner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Congress_of_Berlin,_13_July_1878,_by_Anton_von_Werner.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
